// Sweeping one held dig along a face where two materials the pickaxe can't cut alternate (granite with iron
// ore in it) says each refusal once, not every time the cursor crosses from one to the other: each line
// waits 5 s before it is said again. (Before, only the last line was remembered, so the two lines took turns
// about four times a second; found by the `progression` example.)
map
BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..........##ii##ii##..........#
#.....@....##ii##ii##..........#
################################
end
mode survival
tool 1 1
// one continuous press, the cursor moving back and forth between granite and iron ore every 1/4 s
mine 10-24 5 0
mine 25-39 7 0
mine 40-54 5 0
mine 55-69 7 0
mine 70-84 5 0
mine 85-99 7 0
mine 100-114 5 0
mine 115-129 7 0
expect 130 log:granite_is_too_hard == 1
expect 130 log:iron_ore_is_too_hard == 1
expect 130 ev:Crack >= 2              // each change of material still clinks (it's a new face)
